          "content": "Brilliant idea! Let's add **Custom Application Settings** for employers when posting jobs. Here's how we'll implement it:\n\n## 🎯 Employer-Controlled Application Requirements\n\n### **1. Add to Job Schema** (Backend)\n\n```typescript\n// convex/schema.ts - Add to jobs table\njobs: defineTable({\n  // ... existing fields\n  \n  // Application Requirements (NEW)\n  applicationSettings: v.optional(v.object({\n    // Required fields (always collected)\n    requireResume: v.boolean(), // default: true\n    requireCoverLetter: v.boolean(), // default: false\n    \n    // Optional fields\n    requirePortfolio: v.boolean(), // default: false\n    requireLinkedIn: v.boolean(), // default: false\n    requireAvailability: v.boolean(), // default: false\n    requireSalaryExpectations: v.boolean(), // default: false\n    requireWorkAuthorization: v.boolean(), // default: false\n    requireWillingToRelocate: v.boolean(), // default: false\n    \n    // Custom questions (up to 5)\n    customQuestions: v.optional(v.array(v.object({\n      question: v.string(),\n      type: v.union(\n        v.literal(\"text\"), // Short text\n        v.literal(\"textarea\"), // Long text\n        v.literal(\"select\"), // Dropdown\n        v.literal(\"radio\"), // Multiple choice\n        v.literal(\"checkbox\"), // Checkboxes\n        v.literal(\"file\") // File upload\n      ),\n      required: v.boolean(),\n      options: v.optional(v.array(v.string())), // For select/radio/checkbox\n      maxLength: v.optional(v.number()), // For text fields\n    }))),\n    \n    // Additional settings\n    allowMultipleResumes: v.boolean(), // default: false\n    maxFileSize: v.number(), // in MB, default: 5\n    acceptedFileTypes: v.array(v.string()), // [\"pdf\", \"docx\", \"doc\"]\n  })),\n}))\n```\n\n### **2. Job Posting Flow** (Employer Side)\n\nAdd a new step in `/employer-dashboard/jobs/new`:\n\n```\nStep 1: Job Details\nStep 2: Requirements & Skills\nStep 3: Application Settings (NEW) ← Configure what to collect\nStep 4: Review & Publish\n```\n\n**Application Settings UI**:\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Application Requirements                                 │\n│ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │\n│                                                          │\n│ Required Information:                                    │\n│ ☑ Resume/CV (always required)                           │\n│ ☐ Cover Letter                                          │\n│ ☐ Portfolio/Work Samples                                │\n│ ☐ LinkedIn Profile URL                                  │\n│                                                          │\n│ Additional Questions:                                    │\n│ ☐ Availability to start                                 │\n│ ☐ Salary expectations                                   │\n│ ☐ Work authorization status                             │\n│ ☐ Willing to relocate                                   │\n│                                                          │\n│ Custom Questions: [+ Add Question]                      │\n│ ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n│ │ 1. Why do you want to work at our company?        │ │\n│ │    Type: [Long Text ▼]  Required: ☑               │ │\n│ │    [Remove]                                        │ │\n│ └────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │\n│                                                          │\n│ ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n│ │ 2. Years of experience with React?                │ │\n│ │    Type: [Dropdown ▼]  Required: ☑                │ │\n│ │    Options: 0-1, 1-3, 3-5, 5+                     │ │\n│ │    [Remove]                                        │ │\n│ └────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │\n│                                                          │\n│ File Upload Settings:                                    │\n│ • Max file size: [5 MB ▼]                               │\n│ • Accepted formats: ☑ PDF  ☑ DOCX  ☐ DOC               │\n│ • Allow multiple resumes: ☐                             │\n│                                                          │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### **3. Dynamic Application Form** (Job Seeker Side)\n\nThe `/dashboard/jobs/[id]/apply` page will:\n\n1. **Fetch job's applicationSettings**\n2. **Dynamically render form fields** based on settings\n3. **Validate based on required fields**\n\n**Example Flow**:\n\n```typescript\n// Fetch job settings\nconst job = useQuery(api.jobs.get, { id: jobId });\nconst settings = job?.applicationSettings;\n\n// Dynamic form structure\nconst formSteps = [\n  {\n    title: \"Personal Details\",\n    fields: [\"name\", \"email\", \"phone\", \"location\"] // Always required\n  },\n  {\n    title: \"Resume & Documents\",\n    fields: [\n      settings?.requireResume && \"resume\",\n      settings?.requirePortfolio && \"portfolio\",\n      settings?.requireCoverLetter && \"coverLetter\",\n    ].filter(Boolean)\n  },\n  {\n    title: \"Additional Information\",\n    fields: [\n      settings?.requireLinkedIn && \"linkedInUrl\",\n      settings?.requireAvailability && \"availability\",\n      settings?.requireSalaryExpectations && \"salaryExpectations\",\n      settings?.requireWorkAuthorization && \"workAuthorization\",\n      settings?.requireWillingToRelocate && \"willingToRelocate\",\n    ].filter(Boolean)\n  },\n  settings?.customQuestions?.length > 0 && {\n    title: \"Additional Questions\",\n    fields: settings.customQuestions.map((q, i) => `custom_${i}`)\n  },\n  {\n    title: \"Review & Submit\",\n    fields: []\n  }\n].filter(Boolean);\n```\n\n### **4. Benefits of This Approach**:\n\n✅ **Flexibility**: Each employer customizes their application process\n✅ **Relevance**: Only collect what's needed for that specific role\n✅ **Compliance**: Can add legal questions (work authorization, etc.)\n✅ **Screening**: Custom questions help pre-screen candidates\n✅ **Professional**: Matches LinkedIn, Indeed, Greenhouse ATS\n\n### **5. Default Settings** (If employer doesn't customize):\n\n```typescript\nconst defaultSettings = {\n  requireResume: true,\n  requireCoverLetter: false,\n  requirePortfolio: false,\n  requireLinkedIn: false,\n  requireAvailability: false,\n  requireSalaryExpectations: false,\n  requireWorkAuthorization: false,\n  requireWillingToRelocate: false,\n  customQuestions: [],\n  allowMultipleResumes: false,\n  maxFileSize: 5,\n  acceptedFileTypes: [\"pdf\", \"docx\"]\n};\n```\n\n### **6. Example Custom Questions**:\n\n- \"Why do you want to work at [Company]?\" (Long text)\n- \"Years of experience with [Technology]?\" (Dropdown: 0-1, 1-3, 3-5, 5+)\n- \"Are you comfortable with on-call rotations?\" (Yes/No)\n- \"Upload code sample\" (File upload)\n- \"Preferred work arrangement?\" (Radio: Remote, Hybrid, On-site)\n\n---\n\n**Should I proceed with implementing this?** \n\nThis will give you a **massive competitive advantage** - most job boards have static application forms, but you'll have dynamic, employer-customizable applications like enterprise ATS systems! 🚀"
